#!/usr/bin/env python
r"""
install_bloodfest_update5.py - UPDATES an existing Bloodfest project in place (v5 -> v6).

Adds
  * Four heroes: Storm Ranger, Night Reaper, Wild Druid and Arc Artificer. Each has Q/W/E/R.
  * Four weighted random farm enemies per camp/respawn: Goblin Raider (35%), Ogre Brute (20%),
    Bone Archer (25%), Chaos Wisp (20%). Types have different HP, attack, armor, speed and range.
  * Tougher enemy types pay proportionally more gold and XP.
  * Distinct browser-drawn art for every new hero and enemy; no image downloads.
  * Compact enemy variant ids raise the conservative full-room estimate to ~0.092 GB/hour uncompressed.
    Database and all free-tier guards remain unchanged.

Requires updates 1 through 4 to be applied already.

Usage (PowerShell, from the Bloodfest folder or its parent)
    python install_bloodfest_update5.py --dry-run     # show what would change, write nothing
    python install_bloodfest_update5.py               # apply
    python install_bloodfest_update5.py --test        # apply, then run the test suite in .venv
    python install_bloodfest_update5.py --dir "C:\Python Projects\Bloodfest"
    python install_bloodfest_update5.py --overwrite-mismatched   # replace files whose changes don't fit

Safety
  * Everything is computed in memory first. If any required change does not fit, NOTHING is written.
  * Already-applied changes are detected and skipped, so re-running is harmless.
  * Every file that changes is copied to .installer_backups\<timestamp>\ first.
  * Python / JSON / JavaScript results are syntax-checked before anything is written.
  * Windows (CRLF) and Unix (LF) line endings are both handled and preserved.
"""
